{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013xJ2zbcAVCBL1PMY8R93wH","type":"tool_result","content":"commit 4716a44987d2b10924efa096edda81a317ee97b3\nAuthor: Carlo Jae Avila <cjaee.avila@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Oct 13 23:11:15 2026 +0800\n\n    Keep literal GM answer values out of workflow/lib docstrings (fair-run hygiene)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018p99ADyg71xz9u95Z7uYqD\n\n hctf/fmtalt.py | 2 +-\n lib/slug.py    | 4 ++--\n 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\ncommit 4716a44987d2b10924efa096edda81a317ee97b3\nAuthor: Carlo Jae Avila <cjaee.avila@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Oct 13 23:11:15 2026 +0800\n\n    Keep literal GM answer values out of workflow/lib docstrings (fair-run hygiene)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018p99ADyg71xz9u95Z7uYqD\n\ndiff --git a/hctf/fmtalt.py b/hctf/fmtalt.py\nindex 434bf59..c53bd33 100644\n--- a/hctf/fmtalt.py\n+++ b/hctf/fmtalt.py\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n The metadata worker had the right value by T+16-20 on D10 and D13 and still lost ~20 s each to its spelling: D10 an\n entry-point RVA not zero-padded to the 8-digit struct width (`0x65bd0` -> `0x00065bd0`), D13 an MSI ProductCode\n-stripped of its braces (`DD1A80D5-...` -> `{DD1A80D5-...}`). The value's SHAPE + the field id say which renderings\n+stripped of its braces (`XXXXXXXX-...` -> `{XXXXXXXX-...}`). The value's SHAPE + the field id say which renderings\n exist; probing <= 3 of them costs ~1 s each inside the worker's own submit call, instead of an LLM retry turn.\n \n   alternates(aid, value, q, exclude=())  ->  [(alt_value, transform_name), ...]  best first\ndiff --git a/lib/slug.py b/lib/slug.py\nindex 55ef329..ad78bef 100644\n--- a/lib/slug.py\n+++ b/lib/slug.py\n@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@\n \"\"\"Answer-slug plausibility (warmups `word-word-word-NN`): is a decoded slug made of real words?\n \n The GM's slug generator draws from a CLOSED vocabulary (154 words over D1-D13; no new word since D8), so a slug whose\n-words are neither generator words nor English is a mis-decode -- e.g. D13's reuse race submitted the rot-N reading\n-'ovisx-tviskr-fbvecw-31' of Atbash text (true: 'handy-candle-quartz-31') and burned a GM submission on it.\n+words are neither generator words nor English is a mis-decode -- e.g. D13's reuse race submitted a rot-N reading of\n+Atbash text (three non-words + NN) and burned a GM submission on it.\n \n   VOCAB    lib/refs/slug_words.txt (shipped, built from GM-confirmed slugs) + every slug word found at runtime in\n            challenges/*/warmups*/**/{confirmed,expected}.json (cached once per process)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c15d1ac-3029-4a6e-a501-11867199be60","uuid":"c825d71d-c69c-4f41-8e2c-c20c89cc8827","timestamp":"2026-10-14T13:12:13.869Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 4716a44987d2b10924efa096edda81a317ee97b3\nAuthor: Carlo Jae Avila <cjaee.avila@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Oct 13 23:11:15 2026 +0800\n\n    Keep literal GM answer values out of workflow/lib docstrings (fair-run hygiene)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018p99ADyg71xz9u95Z7uYqD\n\n hctf/fmtalt.py | 2 +-\n lib/slug.py    | 4 ++--\n 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\ncommit 4716a44987d2b10924efa096edda81a317ee97b3\nAuthor: Carlo Jae Avila <cjaee.avila@gmail.com>\nDate:   Tue Oct 13 23:11:15 2026 +0800\n\n    Keep literal GM answer values out of workflow/lib docstrings (fair-run hygiene)\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018p99ADyg71xz9u95Z7uYqD\n\ndiff --git a/hctf/fmtalt.py b/hctf/fmtalt.py\nindex 434bf59..c53bd33 100644\n--- a/hctf/fmtalt.py\n+++ b/hctf/fmtalt.py\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n The metadata worker had the right value by T+16-20 on D10 and D13 and still lost ~20 s each to its spelling: D10 an\n entry-point RVA not zero-padded to the 8-digit struct width (`0x65bd0` -> `0x00065bd0`), D13 an MSI ProductCode\n-stripped of its braces (`DD1A80D5-...` -> `{DD1A80D5-...}`). The value's SHAPE + the field id say which renderings\n+stripped of its braces (`XXXXXXXX-...` -> `{XXXXXXXX-...}`). The value's SHAPE + the field id say which renderings\n exist; probing <= 3 of them costs ~1 s each inside the worker's own submit call, instead of an LLM retry turn.\n \n   alternates(aid, value, q, exclude=())  ->  [(alt_value, transform_name), ...]  best first\ndiff --git a/lib/slug.py b/lib/slug.py\nindex 55ef329..ad78bef 100644\n--- a/lib/slug.py\n+++ b/lib/slug.py\n@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@\n \"\"\"Answer-slug plausibility (warmups `word-word-word-NN`): is a decoded slug made of real words?\n \n The GM's slug generator draws from a CLOSED vocabulary (154 words over D1-D13; no new word since D8), so a slug whose\n-words are neither generator words nor English is a mis-decode -- e.g. D13's reuse race submitted the rot-N reading\n-'ovisx-tviskr-fbvecw-31' of Atbash text (true: 'handy-candle-quartz-31') and burned a GM submission on it.\n+words are neither generator words nor English is a mis-decode -- e.g. D13's reuse race submitted a rot-N reading of\n+Atbash text (three non-words + NN) and burned a GM submission on it.\n \n   VOCAB    lib/refs/slug_words.txt (shipped, built from GM-confirmed slugs) + every slug word found at runtime in\n            challenges/*/warmups*/**/{confirmed,expected}.json (cached once per process)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013xJ2zbcAVCBL1PMY8R93wH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
